// Romantic Comedy: original stories written for this game. Format: docs/v3/BLUEPRINT-FORMAT.md.

== romantic-comedy.f01 | feature | three-act
title: Subject To Availability
genre: romantic-comedy + comedy
tone: Warm, quick and a little rueful, with jokes that come from competence
era: - | contemporary
setting: Glasgow | real | city
logline: A wedding planner who has never been late and a ferry engineer who has never made a plan are stranded together by a storm with another couple's entire wedding in the back of a van.
premise: {priya} runs weddings to the minute and has built her business on never needing a favour. {callum} keeps a fifty-year-old island ferry running with parts he makes himself and has not booked anything in advance since his own wedding was called off. Her van, his ferry and a storm put the two of them in charge of getting a marquee, a cake and a harpist to the island of Gigha by Saturday noon.
synopsis: {priya} arrives at the slip at Tayinloan with a van full of wedding and four minutes in hand, to find the ferry tied up and {callum} underneath it. The sailing is cancelled for weather; he says tomorrow, perhaps. She has a bride, {isla}, who has already postponed once and a mother of the bride, {moira}, who is counting. {priya} sets out to organise the storm: alternative boats, a helicopter quote, a schedule on the van door. {callum} takes it apart item by item, kindly, and then fixes what can be fixed with what is to hand. They move the cake into a fishmonger's cold store, rehearse the harpist in a pub, and discover that the groom, {dougie}, is {callum}'s oldest friend, the best man at the wedding {callum}'s own bride never came to, who has not spoken to him since. Over a night of small rescues {priya} learns to ask and {callum} learns to promise: he tells her he will sail at six, and writes it down. At six the engine will not turn. He cannot keep the first promise he has made in three years, and {priya}, instead of producing plan D, sits down on the slip and laughs. They get the wedding across in four fishing boats lashed in a line, with the marquee as a sail cover and {moira} at a tiller. The ceremony starts at noon by the island's clock, which {callum} has set back twenty minutes. {priya} misses her next booking. She stays for the dancing.
question: Can someone who trusts only her own plans and someone who trusts no plans at all make one promise to each other and keep it?
themes: control as a way of not needing people; improvising as a way of not hoping; what a promise is for
audience: Adults who like their romance earned through a shared job
viewpoint: Mostly with {priya}, slipping to {callum} when she is out of the room
stakes: {isla}'s wedding, twice postponed, will not survive a third; {priya}'s firm lives on its record; {callum} is one failed inspection from losing the ferry
conflict: Her need to control every hour against his refusal to promise anything, with a tide table in charge of both
ending: The wedding lands at noon on a clock {callum} has put back. {priya} lets her phone ring out and dances. He asks her what she is doing a week on Thursday, and has already written it down.
experience: The pleasure of watching two capable people be bad at the same thing in opposite ways, then good at it together
look: Slate sea and a yellow van; everything wet and bright. Lists everywhere: on doors, hands, the back of a tide table
sound: Rain on a van roof, rigging, a harp heard through a pub wall; ceilidh music only at the end
m: belong | self | safety-vs-freedom | reconciled
@ priya | Priya Raghunathan | lead | protagonist | human | she/her | 34 | To deliver this wedding on time and owe nobody | Her parents' shop went under on other people's promises | A storm she cannot reschedule | Brilliant at anticipating everyone's needs except her own | From never asking to asking well | Fast, numbered points, says "right" when she means "help" | Waterproofs over a good suit, a headset she forgets she is wearing
@ callum | Callum MacSween | lead | love-interest | human | he/him | 37 | To keep the ferry running one more season | It is the last thing his father built | The engine, the inspector and his own rule against promising | Can fix anything except a date | From "perhaps" to "six o'clock, I'll be there" | Slow, exact, undersells everything | Boiler suit, oil to the elbows, reading glasses on a bootlace
@ isla | Isla Drummond | supporting | ally | human | she/her | 29 | To be married on the island her gran was married on | She has cancelled once for her mother's sake | Weather, and the fear that it is a sign | Calm for everyone else, terrified privately | From waiting for permission to deciding | Gentle, then suddenly blunt | Wedding hair under a bobble hat
@ dougie | Dougie Farquhar | supporting | foil | human | he/him | 36 | To make it right with {callum} before he marries | He was best man at the wedding that didn't happen and never said sorry | Three years of not phoning | Loud, loyal and a coward about one thing | From avoiding to apologising | Banter, nicknames, then quiet | Rugby build in a kilt he can't fasten
@ moira | Moira Drummond | featured | rival | human | she/her | 61 | For it to be perfect, meaning hers | Her own wedding was in a registry office in the rain | She is not in charge and knows it | Critical of everything, first to roll her sleeves up | From counting faults to steering a boat | Sighs, lists, unexpected swearing | Fascinator pinned through a rain hood
~ priya - callum | planner and the man with the boat | she schedules him, he declines | a date in his handwriting
~ callum - dougie | friends since school, silent for three years | {dougie} can't look at him | an apology shouted across open water
~ priya - moira | supplier and the client's mother | {moira} checks her work | {moira} takes orders from her, once
~ isla - moira | daughter and mother | {isla} asks her mother's leave | {isla} tells her to get in the boat
# Opening | EXT | Tayinloan Ferry Slip | DAY | priya, callum | Meet at cross purposes | {priya} reverses the van to the ramp with four minutes spare; a hand comes out from under the ferry and asks for a seventeen-mil spanner. Sailing cancelled | | 4 | vehicles=van+ferry, water, props=spanner+clipboard
# Opening | INT | Harbour Cafe | DAY | priya, isla, moira | Set the clock | {priya} briefs the bride and her mother with a laminated schedule; {moira} produces her own. Noon Saturday or the registrar goes home | | 3 | props=laminated schedule
# Development | INT | Fishmonger's Cold Store | NIGHT | priya, callum | First small rescue | Four tiers of cake between boxes of langoustine. He rigs a shelf from fish crates; she labels it. They are good at this | She asks him for something | 4 | props=wedding cake+fish crates
# Development | INT | Harbour Bar | NIGHT | priya, callum, dougie, isla | The past walks in | The harpist rehearses in the snug. {dougie} sees {callum} and drops a tray; {isla} tells {priya} the story of the wedding that wasn't | {priya} learns why he won't promise | 5 | props=harp, crowd=20
# Escalation | INT | Ferry Engine Room | NIGHT | priya, callum | The promise | She holds the torch; he explains the engine like a relative. She asks him to say a time. He writes "0600" on the tide table and signs it | | 5 | props=tide table+torch
# Escalation | EXT | Tayinloan Ferry Slip | DAWN | priya, callum, moira | The promise breaks | Six o'clock. The engine turns over twice and stops. {moira} starts counting faults; {priya} opens her mouth to produce a plan, and laughs instead | {priya} has no plan D | 4 | vehicles=ferry, water
# Climax | EXT | The Sound Of Gigha | DAY | priya, callum, dougie, isla, moira | Cross anyway | Four fishing boats in a line, marquee over the cake, harp wrapped in oilskins, {moira} steering. {dougie} shouts his apology from the next boat and {callum} shouts back to mind the cake | {callum} accepts it | 7 | water, vehicles=four fishing boats, stunts=open-water crossing, crowd=12, props=marquee+harp+cake
# Resolution | EXT | Gigha Churchyard | DAY | priya, callum, isla, dougie, moira | Land it | The island clock says five to twelve. {priya} checks her watch, looks at {callum}, and says nothing. The vows | | 4 | crowd=60, props=church clock
# Resolution | INT | Village Hall | NIGHT | priya, callum | Stay | Her phone rings on a windowsill. He shows her the tide table: a week on Thursday, in ink. She goes back to the dancing | | 3 | dance, crowd=60, props=tide table
